            "image_caption": ""
          }
        },
        "reason_4": {
          "type": "benefit",
          "settings": {
            "category": "SIDE EFFECTS & COMFORT",
            "heading": "Concerned About Side Effects? Know Exactly What You're Taking",
            "body": "<p>When you are already managing a complicated wellness routine, the last thing you want is a supplement with a long list of mystery ingredients. Comfort, clarity and confidence matter when something becomes part of your day.</p><p><strong>Avonent keeps its featured ingredients clearly identified:</strong> true Ceylon cinnamon, berberine HCl and MCT oil—without hiding them behind a proprietary blend. No supplement can promise zero side effects, and berberine may interact with medicines, so check with your healthcare professional if you take prescriptions.</p>",
            "highlight": "A clearly labeled formula without the mystery",
            "image_alt": "Avonent Ceylon cinnamon ingredient photograph",
            "image_caption": ""
          }
        },
        "reason_5": {
          "type": "benefit",
          "settings": {
            "category": "AUTHENTIC CEYLON",
            "heading": "Not Cheap Grocery-Store Cassia. Real Ceylon Cinnamon.",
            "body": "<p>Not all cinnamon is the same. Many everyday cinnamon products use Cassia, a different variety that naturally contains more coumarin. True Ceylon cinnamon (<em>Cinnamomum verum</em>) is known for its delicate layered quills and typically much lower coumarin content.</p><p><strong>We chose the variety on purpose.</strong> Avonent identifies authentic Ceylon cinnamon in the formula instead of asking you to trust a generic 'cinnamon' label. When you take something daily, details like the plant variety matter.</p>",
            "highlight": "True Ceylon cinnamon—not an unspecified substitute",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/99A8FC23-1F52-4CC7-A154-36FC53C085C0.png",
            "image_alt": "Avonent Ceylon cinnamon ingredient photograph",
            "image_caption": ""
          }
        },
        "reason_6": {
          "type": "benefit",
          "settings": {
            "category": "CLINICALLY STUDIED INGREDIENTS",
            "heading": "It's Not Just Natural. The Ingredients Have Been Studied.",
            "body": "<p>There is a reason cinnamon and berberine keep appearing in conversations about metabolic health. Researchers have studied these ingredients for their potential roles in glucose metabolism and insulin response, with results that vary across studies and individuals.</p><p><strong>Avonent makes the formula easy to evaluate:</strong> 1,200 mg Ceylon cinnamon, 400 mg berberine HCl and 200 mg MCT oil per listed daily serving. We believe real ingredient transparency matters more than inflated claims. Ingredient research is not the same as a clinical trial of the finished Avonent product.</p>",
